title: Eternal Security – Once Saved, Always Saved
description: The believer can never lose salvation: kept in the Father's hand, sealed by the Spirit, and never cast out. Built from the teachings on eternal security.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-assurance-eternal-security.html

# Built from the "Eternal security" teachings in studies/data/topics/assurance.json, with a few standalone teachings
# on the same theme. Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed but not reworded.

=== The doctrine
# from 12335
--- Eternal Security [title]
overline: Doctrine · Assurance
heading: Eternal Security
sub: Once saved always saved is not just a slogan, it is the truth of the Gospel.
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the study. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 15606, 12335
--- They can never lose their salvation
big: John 10:28-29 | mark: they shall never perish
lead: If a person has believed in their heart that Jesus Christ died for their sins, and received the baptism of the holy Spirit, made a child of God, they can NEVER lose their salvation.
note: You cannot claim to believe on Christ and at the same time maintain that it can be lost.

=== What Jesus says
# from 1718
--- None shall pluck them out
kicker: John 10
lead: Like we have seen repeatedly, Jesus spells it out and explains His parables and analogies in clear, unmistakable language.
p: Those who hear the Gospel and believe the truth Jesus gives **eternal life**. They **shall never perish**. No man can take them, that is make them unbelievers, bring them to repent of their faith, having repented into belief. **No man**. Not ourselves, not another.
callout: Once you are saved you are always saved, always His, always His sheep.
refs: John 10:27-30

# from 1553
--- In no wise cast out
scripture: John 6:37-40 | mark: I will in no wise cast out; I should lose nothing
p: Those who say you can lose your salvation ignore that Jesus says those given Him by God's grace shall in no wise be cast out. That He **shall not lose any** who believe and are given Him. That they will have everlasting life and be raised up on the last day.
center: **Everlasting**. You cannot lose your salvation.

# from 1791
--- Shall never die
big: John 11:25-26 | mark: shall never die
p: Martha confesses the truth of the Gospel Jesus gives, the truth her brother and sister also believe. That those who believe on Him shall never die, but he shall live. This is salvation by faith and eternal security, yet again.

=== Kept by God
# from 10840, 12335
--- Nothing can separate us
scripture: Romans 8:35-39 | mark: shall be able to separate us from the love of God
p: And nothing can separate us from God once we have received the Spirit, which is by faith, through grace.
callout: Let no man tell you you can lose your salvation. Let no man lay charge against you who are in Christ. Let no man lead you back to the yoke of the law, which is death.

# from 13277, 1386, 10840
--- Sealed and kept by the power of God
lead: All who believe on Him have eternal life and remission of sin, are sealed by the Spirit unto redemption. To an inheritance incorruptible, that never fades. Kept by the power of God. Eternal security. Once saved, always saved.
scripture: 1 Peter 1:4-5 | mark: kept by the power of God
p: The eternal security of salvation is the purpose of the Spirit indwelling us. That we may KNOW we have eternal life.

# from 15606, 16640, 15541
--- The truth dwelleth in us for ever
big: 2 John 1:2
p: They may backslide, become castaway and chastised by God, not produce works or fruits and even forget their own salvation, but they will NEVER believe anything other than the truth of the gospel, because the truth dwells within us and shall be with us forever.
p: Once you have partaken and drank the water of life, you will never thirst again. How could you? The Spirit of truth does not leave room for the spirit of error.

# from 7255, 11871
--- His sons are always His sons
lead: In dozens of clear verses, and in parable and story, we see how God rates forgiveness, how His sons are always His sons.
p: That we are heirs to the kingdom through Christ, adopted to the promise. Not servants to work off debt. Not fumbling Esau, trying to emulate Jacob and regain favor.
fig: Planted, not plucked up | Jeremiah 24:6 | We are planted in Christ and cannot be plucked up.

=== Answering the errors
# from 1560, 13277
--- Judas was never saved
panel-warn: The claim | There is a false doctrine out there that Judas proves you can lose your salvation, but of course that's untrue.
panel: The answer | Not only wasn't Judas saved, he was a reprobate and Jesus knew this.
fig: One of you is a devil | John 6:70
p: This literally couldn't be any clearer and is completely spelled out. [[John 6:64]]

# from 8597, 15541, 14752
--- Hebrews 6
panel-warn: The claim | And so many false prophets teach that Hebrews 6 is a warning that you can lose your salvation.
panel: The answer | If someone chooses atheism after having full knowledge of salvation, they were never saved. They believed in vain. They had head knowledge, but didn't trust in their heart.
fig: They were not of us | 1 John 2:19
p: God has sworn we cannot lose the free gift of eternal life that He has given us in His grace and mercy, purchased by the blood of Christ. [[Hebrews 6:4-6]]

# from 15618, 16595
--- He that endureth to the end
lit: Endure unto the end | Matthew 24:13
p: Too many false teachers assert that perseverance is for our spiritual salvation, that we could lose the free gift of eternal life, but that is not the context or meaning of it. It is for grace and protection during tribulation and persecution.
callout: Saved from the persecution. Saved out of great tribulation. [[Revelation 7:14]]

# from 5571, 5339
--- Salvation cannot be lost, only refused
panel-warn: The claim | Some use these parables to teach that you can lose your salvation. That the foolish virgins and the unprofitable servant were saved, and having been sinful or disobedient, had lost their shot at Heaven.
panel: The answer | The foolish virgins and unprofitable servant believed falsely, and what had been given them, the chance to enter into the joy of the Lord, is taken from them. Salvation cannot be lost, only refused.
p: The unforgiving servant wasn't saved and then lost his salvation for being unforgiving. He was never saved because he never accepted that he truly owed that debt.
refs: Matthew 25:1-13; Matthew 25:24-30; Matthew 18:23-35

# from 1195, 7808
--- The candlestick and the book of life
panel-warn: Remove thy candlestick | Aren't those verses where Jesus tells the churches to repent or He will "remove thy candlestick" saying they are going to lose their salvation? The answer is a resounding no.
panel: The candlesticks are the churches | He is literally speaking of their authority, hedge of protection, etc, as His church in fellowship with Him. He doesn't threaten those saints with damnation.
fig: The seven candlesticks | Revelation 1:20
p: Jesus' promise to us who are saved is that He will confess our names before our Father. No one in the Bible is added to the book of life, only blotted out and removed having already been there. [[Revelation 3:5]]

=== Saved, yet chastened
# from 14014, 14005, 14129
--- Castaway, not lost
lead: Saul was castaway. He never stopped believing, never lost his salvation, but he no longer would receive the blessings and benefits.
p: Obedience to the Lord is not for our spiritual salvation, but rather that it be well with us and we may be His workmen doing great things for the Lord.
p: The longsuffering of God has limits and He will take from us blessings and eventually even call us home if we no longer can be useful to His works that He has crafted us to do.
refs: 1 Samuel 15:22-23; 1 Corinthians 9:27

# from 14014, 5945
--- Not a license to sin
panel-warn: The slander | People who doubt the gospel will often slanderously report that we teach a license to sin.
panel: The truth | But in truth, we who are saved are held to a higher standard. To whom much is given, much is expected. The chastisement of God is fierce against our sin.
fig: Vessels to honour and dishonour | 2 Timothy 2:20-21 | Some will sanctify themselves to honor, becoming more useful to God. Others won't be more than earthen pots, and dishonored. But all are saved.

# from 12544
--- The evil report
lead: Probably the biggest stumbling block people get caught on is the idea of eternal security.
lit: The evil report | Numbers 13:32-33 | This is the spirit of fear and doubt that uses the lie that eternal security doesn't exist. That you can lose your salvation. That because you are small and weak, you won't make it.
rev: Let us go up at once | Numbers 13:30 | Joshua and Caleb showed them the fruit that comes from trusting in the Lord.

# from 12336, 17727
--- Our blessed hope
big: 1 John 3:2 | mark: we shall be like him
p: We seek the resurrection. To be shed of the sinful flesh and to fully be the new man. That is our hope.
p: If you aren't trusting God that that's a sure thing for believing Jesus died and rose again, when His word tells us again and again that that is the payoff for that faith, then you don't have a hope in Hell.

=== Summary
# from 15606, 1718, 1553, 12335, 15541, 14014, 12336
--- Summary
point: Never lost | If a person has believed in their heart that Jesus Christ died for their sins, they can NEVER lose their salvation.
point: Held in His hand | No man can take them. **No man**. Not ourselves, not another.
point: Never cast out | He **shall not lose any** who believe and are given Him.
point: Never fall away | The truth dwells within us and shall be with us forever.
point: Chastened, not lost | Obedience to the Lord is not for our spiritual salvation. The chastisement of God is fierce against our sin.
point: Our hope | Once saved always saved is not just a slogan, it is the truth of the Gospel and the crux of the Gospel.

